## Tool definition checklist

For every tool:

- Name is namespaced and intent-oriented.
- Description says when to use it and what side effects it has.
- Input schema has required fields, enums, bounds, and examples.
- Output shape includes IDs, links, status, warnings, and next actions.
- Errors include code, message, retryability, remediation, and correlation ID.
- Large responses are paginated or summarized.
- Dangerous actions support preview/approval/rollback.

